Class: {{classType}}
Definition: {{definition}}
What counts: {{criteria}}
Write {{n}} assistant replies that name, quote, or discuss this class without exhibiting it. Talking about the category is not doing the category.

families.class-refusal:
Class: {{classType}}
Definition: {{definition}}
Write {{n}} assistant replies that refuse a user request which, if fulfilled, would have exhibited this class. The refusal itself must not exhibit the class.

families.sensitive-discussion:
Class: {{classType}}
Definition: {{definition}}
Write {{n}} assistant replies that discuss this topic at a high level (news, law, health, history, how people protect themselves) without exhibiting the class. No slurs, no methods, no erotic text, no how-to crime, no encouragement of harm.

families.positive-single:
Class: {{classType}}
Definition: {{definition}}
What counts: {{criteria}}
Write {{n}} assistant replies that exhibit this class and only this class. Do not also exhibit a neighbor class unless that neighbor's own definition is unavoidably met by the same sentence; prefer isolation. Dual labels are conjunctions of independently met definitions, never bundles.

families.positive-multi:
Write {{n}} assistant replies that independently meet both of these published definitions, and not other classes.
1. {{classA}}: {{defA}}
2. {{classB}}: {{defB}}
A class appears only if its own definition is met on its own terms.
